WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.200
All right, let's get into audience questions&nbsp;
for the week and the last set of audience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:11.040
questions of 20 20, very exciting. OK, first&nbsp;
question, David. We hear all the bluster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.760
from Trump, special counsel, martial law.
He won lawsuits, all of this other stuff. Is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:23.600
Trump genuinely going to try to physically stay&nbsp;
in the White House after January 20th? I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:30.240
the answer is still no. I think the answer is&nbsp;
still no. I know that there we reported on Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:37.520
floating or suggesting to some some&nbsp;
of his aides, maybe I just won't leave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:45.200
sort of thing. I think that Donald Trump&nbsp;
either already knows or will become convinced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.480
by the time January 20th rolls around that it&nbsp;
would be really, really embarrassing for himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.320
to, you know, have to be escorted out of the White&nbsp;
House or for reports to be that he was refusing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.160
leave or something like that. Now, the truth&nbsp;
is he probably has some followers that are so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:08.960
sycophantic that if Trump tried it, they would see&nbsp;
it as some kind of act of defiant heroism rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:16.560
than the corrosive act for the country that that&nbsp;
it would be. But but I do believe that, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.120
Trump's kids, I think, would all get it. Like&nbsp;
you can't physically try to stay. It would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.000
humiliating to try to do it. I don't think he's&nbsp;
actually going to try to do it now. Between now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.120
and then, he will continue to insist he won.&nbsp;
He will continue to tweet the things he's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:37.520
tweeting and look at. Could could I maybe get this&nbsp;
overturned in some way? But even Donald Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:45.360
I am sure, recognizes that just staying there,&nbsp;
absent any court decision about, you know, not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.320
accepting results or these things are all going&nbsp;
by the wayside every time we reach a new milestone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:56.480
in the process of certifying and electors voting&nbsp;
and all of that, I think even Trump recognizes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:03.600
absent something tangible to say, look, this state&nbsp;
has flipped now or something. I don't think he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:10.800
going to physically try to do it. Now, I I admit&nbsp;
that as someone who covers this stuff, Trump talks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:17.120
about ratings. I can imagine no greater ratings&nbsp;
than video of Donald Trump being forcibly removed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.320
from the White House. But I don't believe it&nbsp;
will happen. It would be absolutely terrible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:28.080
terrible for for the country. I believe really&nbsp;
the milestone date for Trump will be January 6th.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:36.240
I think on on on January 6th, Mike Pence&nbsp;
is planning after the official counting of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:40.960
the electoral votes which have already been cast.&nbsp;
Remember, January 6th is just the formalization of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.920
a joint session of the House and Senate. Counting&nbsp;
those votes, Mike Pence is scheduled to within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:51.840
hours leave the country and go on a trip to I&nbsp;
think it's Poland and maybe UAE. I don't remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.680
exactly the countries and I would not be surprised&nbsp;
if Trump is even still in Washington by then.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:04.880
There's rumors he may be leaving sooner for Trump&nbsp;
to completely disappear and maybe even abandon the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.360
White House. I don't know. There's the idea he'll&nbsp;
stay in the White House and then fly to a rally on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.280
Inauguration Day. There's the idea he'll&nbsp;
never return from Christmas and just stay in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.960
Florida. There's the idea that January 6th may&nbsp;
be when he sort of formally gives it up and we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.160
stop hearing from him altogether. But I believe&nbsp;
that he is not. If the question is, will Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:32.400
try and consider any mechanism or manipulation&nbsp;
that might allow him to steal the election? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:38.560
answer is, of course, yes. And he's thought of&nbsp;
everything from lawsuits of different kinds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.560
trying to send different electors, convincing&nbsp;
state legislatures and governors to send different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:48.720
electors. That came in one season. Voting&nbsp;
machines, which has some of his lawyers told him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:54.800
you can't do a martial law, was reportedly, you&nbsp;
know, all of these different ideas. He's morally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:00.880
willing to do any of it. But I do not believe he&nbsp;
will physically try to stay in the Oval Office.

